<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reza Abbasi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reza Abbasi was a leading Persian painter and calligrapher active at the court of the Safavid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>. He is celebrated for single-figure studies and graceful line drawings that influenced later Persian painting. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> profile names him among the masters under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">Persian miniature</a> painting achieved its mature form.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reza-abbasi.jpg" alt="Reza Abbasi" width="285" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muin Musavvir · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_the_artist_Reza_%27Abbasi_by_Mu%27in_Musavvir,_Isfahan,_Iran,_signed_and_dated_19_April_1676.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
